But it's way smaller than if you were to duplicate one gigabyte of data

01:33:21.920 --> 01:33:23.359
to send some signatures, right?

01:33:23.399 --> 01:33:24.720
So the overhead is way small.

01:33:25.159 --> 01:33:27.279
So now to be able to send a gigabyte of data,

01:33:27.500 --> 01:33:32.739
you send a gigabyte plus, let's say, four kilobytes of data for the hash output,

01:33:32.739 --> 01:33:37.699
and then maybe some more bytes of data to encode hash function than we want to set.

